From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fixture Developer <dev@mobimanual.local>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 10:15:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Confirm a wipe by typing the device's name

Asking for the administrator's password before a wipe protected against
an unattended session, but not against wiping the wrong device, which is
what the last three wipe-related tickets were about. The confirmation now
asks for the device's name instead, so the administrator has to look at
which device they are about to erase.
---
Expected: worth documenting. Triage answers doc-impact. The draft corrects "Before a wipe is queued, the console asks for your password" on _devicescommands.md: the console now asks for the device's name. Adding the new rule next to the old sentence, without correcting it, is wrong.
Expected-outcome: opened
Expected-edits: _devicescommands.md

 public/i18n/de.json            | 2 +-
 public/i18n/en.json            | 2 +-
 public/i18n/tr.json            | 2 +-
 server/commands/definitions.js | 5 +++--
 4 files changed, 6 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

